# Frontend requirements

These requirements apply to every frontend page, component, and visual change.
Follow the approved design system unless the user explicitly requests a change.

## Read before designing or implementing

- [app/globals.css](app/globals.css): canonical design tokens and shared styles.
- [app/layout.tsx](app/layout.tsx): global font loading.
- [app/design-system/page.tsx](app/design-system/page.tsx): living reference, available at `/design-system` on the running app.
- Inspect the component being changed and its callers before editing it.

## Required visual language

- **Every title uses Bespoke Stencil Regular at weight 400, normal style.** This includes page, section, card, and dialog titles. Use semantic `h1`–`h6` elements or `.title` for non-heading display text. Preserve semantic heading order.
- Use the existing local `app/fonts/BespokeStencil-Regular.woff2` through `next/font/local` and `--font-title`. Do not substitute another title family, load a different weight, synthesize bold/italic, or override titles with `font-bold`, `font-semibold`, or `italic`.
- All supporting text, including body copy, labels, navigation, and buttons, uses the shared `--font-serif` stack: the self-hosted Source Serif 4 through `--font-source-serif-4`, then Georgia and serif. Keep typography centralized; do not add component-specific font stacks or sans-serif text.
- Preserve the dark plum, warm ivory, and muted rose direction. Use semantic utilities: `bg-background`, `bg-surface`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted`, `text-accent`, `border-border`, and `text-danger`. The token values in `app/globals.css` are the source of truth.
- Establish hierarchy with size and spacing rather than title weight. Use `text-display`, `text-heading`, the existing heading scale, and `.eyebrow` for small section labels.
- Use Tailwind's existing 4px spacing scale. Use `rounded-control` for controls and `rounded-panel` for surfaces. Favor generous space, clear alignment, and restrained decoration.

## Reuse and extension

- Reuse `.button` on native buttons and action links, and `.surface` for bordered panels. Preserve focus, hover, disabled, and reduced-motion behavior. Do not build parallel versions of existing controls.
- Extend shared tokens/styles in `app/globals.css` when a requested feature needs a new reusable pattern. Update `/design-system` and the README alongside changes to the system.
- Apply these requirements to third-party components too. Keep the user's Shape Waves settings intact unless the task changes them; shader color props require literal hex values, so semantic CSS variables cannot be passed to its color parser.
- Keep decorative effects out of the accessibility tree, maintain readable text contrast, visible keyboard focus, responsive layouts, and reduced-motion support.
- Keep the font license with the font. No new UI dependency is needed merely to follow this design system.

## Verification and handoff

- Check that affected titles compute to Bespoke Stencil at weight 400 and that the local font loads.
- For visual changes, inspect desktop and mobile layouts for overflow, readability, and focus behavior. Run lint and a production build for substantive component or shared-style changes; report checks that could not be completed.
- Treat deviations from these requirements as review findings. Include this file when handing off frontend work to another agent.

